		"schema": "Keyed by CANONICAL component (docs/code identity). Figma splits a component into multiple component_sets for performance only; those live under figmaSets with their exact Figma name + key + axes. The agent reasons in canonical name + props; axes resolve to the right figma set key.",
		"resolution": "1) find canonical component by name. 2) match desired props against figmaSets[*].axes. 3) importComponentSetByKeyAsync(key). 4) pick variant child + createInstance(). If no axes match, STOP and report.",
		"naming": "❌ = deprecated, ↳ / 🛟 = helper/subcomponent (only inside parent), (Beta)/(Concept) = maturity.",
		"coreLab": "Concept components live under conceptComponents (typography + the Grid/Container layout primitives, resolved from the 'DB UX - 🧪 Core Lab' library) and in lab-components-catalog.json. Anything beyond the four baseline entries requires user confirmation.",
		"noLocalComponents": "HARD RULE: every instance is imported from a published library (Core Components, Core Lab, DB Theme Icons). Local components inside the working Figma file MUST NOT be used — there is no local fallback and no name-based page scan.",
		"lastKeyVerification": "2026-07-24 — all non-deprecated figmaSets keys import-tested against the live library (83/83 resolve). Note: Figma component keys can drift WITHIN a version name on re-publish (e.g. Drawer was refreshed here), so re-verify per-key — the version string alone is not a reliable freshness signal.",
		"keyRefresh": "To refresh: for each component, pull the current component_set key from the canonical libraryKey (search_design_system scoped, or import-test existing keys) and update figmaSets. The core build stays pinned to these committed keys (deterministic, no Figma dependency at build time)."
	},

